WEBVTT

00:08.509 --> 00:13.514
16 September,
in the year of our Lord 1702.

00:14.348 --> 00:16.892
The wind has favored us on my journey.

00:17.768 --> 00:20.771
The crew informs me
we are soon to make port.

00:21.855 --> 00:24.024
I hear he is a great man.

00:24.525 --> 00:28.070
Please, Lord,
let him be kind and handsome.

00:28.987 --> 00:31.156
And make room in my heart
for his children.

00:32.783 --> 00:35.994
I thought my time for marriage had passed,

00:36.870 --> 00:38.455
but you had other plans.

00:43.502 --> 00:45.379
Today I begin a new life.

00:46.088 --> 00:48.257
I am to wed a leader,

00:48.882 --> 00:49.883
an explorer,

00:49.967 --> 00:52.511
the founder of this island hamlet.

00:53.637 --> 01:00.435
I, Sarah Westcott, shall this day become
Mrs. Richard Warren.

01:02.312 --> 01:03.647
Just missed the fog.

01:04.272 --> 01:05.440
Stroke of luck, I suppose.

01:05.941 --> 01:08.151
No getting in or out once it arrives.

01:08.861 --> 01:09.945
Straight to the church then?

01:12.239 --> 01:13.532
What is he like?

01:13.615 --> 01:15.701
Well, he's the reason we're all here.

01:16.493 --> 01:18.579
Everyone on this island
owes a great debt to that man.

01:19.162 --> 01:22.374
Fore he arrived, it was a place
with nothing but barren dirt.

01:22.457 --> 01:27.045
But today, blossoms on the trees,
food for every hungry mouth, mild winters.

01:28.380 --> 01:29.798
He controls the weather, does he?

01:30.507 --> 01:31.508
What's that?

01:32.259 --> 01:33.886
He controls the weather, does he?

01:35.679 --> 01:36.763
No.

01:37.598 --> 01:40.851
But a cold breeze cuts half as quick

01:40.934 --> 01:43.562
when you've got
a warm home and a strong coat.

01:46.190 --> 01:47.191
Who said that?

01:47.941 --> 01:49.026
Richard Warren.

02:17.262 --> 02:19.264
Have you no kin come with you?

02:20.682 --> 02:21.683
No.

02:22.351 --> 02:24.686
I had resigned myself
to the lot of a spinster.

02:25.187 --> 02:29.608
Perhaps the greater celebration may be me
no longer a charge on my father's purse.

02:29.691 --> 02:33.362
It's a rare blessing
to marry at such an age.

02:34.238 --> 02:36.740
Lucky the island proved too small
to furnish him a wife.

02:36.823 --> 02:39.409
He had no choice
but to look to the mainland.

02:40.160 --> 02:43.997
A man of stature doth require
a goodly wife to order his household.

02:45.415 --> 02:47.626
Is he a man of-of good repute then?

02:53.006 --> 02:54.800
Sarah, my child,

02:54.883 --> 02:59.012
I am Pastor Collins,
shepherd of the flock here on this island.

02:59.096 --> 03:01.640
- Pleased to meet you, Pastor.
- And I, you.

03:01.723 --> 03:02.891
How was your journey?

03:02.975 --> 03:06.228
Well, I… I arrived
in good order, for which I give thanks.

03:06.311 --> 03:10.399
It must seem to you a strange land,
and you a stranger in it,

03:10.941 --> 03:12.818
but know that you have friends here

03:12.901 --> 03:16.905
and the light of God to lift you up
whenever you feel alone.

03:18.532 --> 03:19.783
Thank you, Pastor.

03:22.119 --> 03:27.291
If you are ever in need, do not
think twice to come to me at any hour.

03:27.374 --> 03:30.711
I will do what I can, by God's grace.

03:32.754 --> 03:34.006
I will, Pastor.

03:35.132 --> 03:36.133
Good.

03:41.013 --> 03:44.391
Richard has requested
to be part of the wedding vows.

03:44.975 --> 03:47.144
Something he's written himself.

03:49.104 --> 03:51.523
They are unique.

03:53.609 --> 03:54.610
Unique?

03:56.195 --> 03:59.531
Love is as strong as death.

04:00.699 --> 04:05.913
Many waters cannot quench love,
neither can the floods drown it.

04:05.996 --> 04:09.750
Richard, do you take
this woman to be your lawful wife?

04:15.255 --> 04:16.380
I do.

04:16.464 --> 04:19.927
Sarah, do you take
this man as your lawful husband?

04:20.969 --> 04:23.263
- I do.
- For you, as his helpmeet,

04:23.847 --> 04:25.891
will be bound to him.

04:25.974 --> 04:29.978
You will agree to serve him
as the Reeve Prime of the colony,

04:30.062 --> 04:33.398
the handmaiden
to the Lord Island Protector.

04:37.486 --> 04:38.820
I do. I do.

04:42.824 --> 04:44.117
Thomas,

04:44.201 --> 04:45.369
John,

04:45.452 --> 04:46.453
Cromwell,

04:46.537 --> 04:47.538
Holyoke,

04:47.621 --> 04:48.622
Frances.

04:48.705 --> 04:50.457
Wagon wheel took her finger.

04:50.541 --> 04:52.876
Children, your new mother.

04:56.421 --> 04:58.340
'Tis a blessing to meet you all.

05:00.759 --> 05:01.760
Has she a name?

05:03.846 --> 05:04.888
Mary.

05:06.682 --> 05:07.683
Good name.

05:09.309 --> 05:10.978
But I think she's missing something.

05:15.649 --> 05:18.193
This brooch came from my mother.

05:21.196 --> 05:22.990
Is there one for each of us?

05:27.202 --> 05:30.372
Perhaps the morrow shall yield
further tokens.

05:35.502 --> 05:36.753
At such an hour?

05:44.678 --> 05:46.555
Ensure no harm comes to them.

05:48.807 --> 05:51.310
Have you an errand
that requires my company?

05:51.393 --> 05:53.395
No, I have work that needs doing.

05:55.731 --> 05:56.899
On our wedding night?

05:56.982 --> 05:59.943
The burdens of leadership
ride my shoulders by day and by dark.

06:00.027 --> 06:02.029
See them all laid down to their rest.

06:06.408 --> 06:10.245
I set down these lines
for the first time as a married woman,

06:10.787 --> 06:15.876
though I confess when my mother spoke
of what to expect on my wedding night,

06:15.959 --> 06:17.961
she missed the mark.

06:19.004 --> 06:21.423
First, there are five children here.

06:22.174 --> 06:26.261
Second, my husband departed suddenly
with neither a caress nor a kind word.

06:27.471 --> 06:30.891
But Christ asks us not to despair,

06:30.974 --> 06:34.394
and I look with hope
to grow into the duties of a wife.

07:01.463 --> 07:02.464
Richard?

07:10.389 --> 07:11.640
Richard, are you home?

07:20.023 --> 07:21.108
Richard?

07:34.371 --> 07:35.372
Richard?

07:50.012 --> 07:51.096
Leave me be.

08:22.753 --> 08:24.171
You're a watcher.

08:28.967 --> 08:30.135
I'm sorry?

08:31.261 --> 08:33.263
You like to watch other people,

08:33.347 --> 08:35.349
see into their business.

08:36.850 --> 08:38.434
Forgive me, what befell them?

08:39.520 --> 08:41.145
There's a plague upon us.

08:41.647 --> 08:44.483
A violent madness comes over the infected.

08:45.734 --> 08:47.069
Can they not be healed?

08:47.569 --> 08:49.029
Well, that's my husband.

08:49.738 --> 08:50.739
Town physician.

08:50.822 --> 08:52.199
He does what he can for them,

08:52.783 --> 08:54.701
gives them something to calm their nerves,

08:54.785 --> 08:56.870
but heal them? No.

08:57.704 --> 08:58.705
But don't worry.

08:59.456 --> 09:03.460
Richard Warren always says
the bad times will end.

09:05.212 --> 09:06.839
God be with you.

09:08.924 --> 09:09.925
And with you.

09:17.099 --> 09:20.060
There's three more infected
this week since the fog.

09:20.143 --> 09:21.687
That makes 20 now in total.

09:23.063 --> 09:25.732
I have warned them
to stay out of the foul air.

09:26.233 --> 09:28.443
Otis Stevens tends to the sick every day.

09:29.778 --> 09:31.029
But he's not infected.

09:31.113 --> 09:32.614
Well, not yet.

09:33.532 --> 09:36.577
They say they suffer
from some kind of mania.

09:37.369 --> 09:38.662
Should we be worried?

09:40.455 --> 09:41.456
No.

09:44.710 --> 09:47.754
Cornelius Evans was the first to fall ill.

09:48.297 --> 09:50.132
At first, had no symptoms
beyond a headache.

09:50.841 --> 09:53.135
His wife gave him brandy.
He slept soundly, but…

09:53.635 --> 09:57.264
he woke always with
the same headache. Here.

09:59.141 --> 10:00.684
Five days like this.

10:01.476 --> 10:03.312
And his eyes
were yellow with spoiled moons.

10:03.395 --> 10:04.396
He changed.

10:04.479 --> 10:05.981
He was angry, confused.

10:06.064 --> 10:07.232
Otis saw him that very night.

10:07.316 --> 10:08.650
He told him to take a warm bath,

10:08.734 --> 10:10.819
and he thought to come back
with a draught in the morning.

10:11.486 --> 10:13.906
But by dawn, when Otis came back,

10:14.823 --> 10:17.159
he saw a knot of hair in the doorway.

10:18.202 --> 10:22.206
Went inside
and he found Cornelius on the ground.

10:24.041 --> 10:26.752
With his fingers inside his wife's skull.

10:33.091 --> 10:35.093
The infections are growing faster.

10:35.677 --> 10:37.679
It will soon overwhelm us.

10:37.763 --> 10:39.097
We must do something.

10:39.181 --> 10:41.475
- You must do something.
- Sarah,

10:41.558 --> 10:43.894
would you take yourself to bed?

10:45.687 --> 10:47.189
But I haven't finished cleaning.

11:00.994 --> 11:03.497
They say that
you're in communion with this island,

11:03.580 --> 11:04.915
that you whisper to it.

11:05.707 --> 11:07.835
You tame it. You turn it to your will.

11:07.918 --> 11:10.379
That you are the only reason we survived

11:10.462 --> 11:12.756
- the first years.
- Hold your tongue.

11:12.840 --> 11:16.635
They say that you kiss
that necklace like it was a cross,

11:16.718 --> 11:18.136
but it's no cross, sir.

11:18.637 --> 11:20.264
What is it you hide in there?

11:20.347 --> 11:21.682
They say it is a covenant!

13:56.837 --> 13:58.630
Child, what ails thee?

14:06.722 --> 14:10.976
I feel I have greatly mistaken
my course in coming here.

14:13.812 --> 14:17.733
Though my days before were sorrowful,
I fared well enough.

14:17.816 --> 14:20.777
Perhaps the life of a…
of a childless woman without a husband,

14:20.861 --> 14:23.155
it is… it is… It is one I could…
I could come to bear…

14:23.238 --> 14:25.908
- Enj… Enjoy! Enjoy the role--
- Good woman, you are not making sense.

14:25.991 --> 14:28.493
Well, I am filled with terror, Pastor!

14:29.036 --> 14:30.287
I saw him.

14:30.370 --> 14:33.040
I saw him murder Ezra Lowery.

14:34.625 --> 14:35.626
Is there a body?

14:35.709 --> 14:36.960
No,

14:37.044 --> 14:39.505
but there's a hidden chamber
beneath our home

14:39.588 --> 14:42.591
and Ezra's bloody cane therein.

14:44.218 --> 14:45.969
You must be told the truth.

14:47.554 --> 14:50.057
Evil stalks this land.

14:50.140 --> 14:52.142
There is a wrongness about.

14:53.769 --> 14:56.939
I fear that the devil himself
has chosen your husband.

14:57.523 --> 14:59.399
For what cause, I cannot tell.

15:00.317 --> 15:01.902
Others share my belief.

15:03.028 --> 15:04.780
We fear Warren consorts with him.

15:06.532 --> 15:08.700
Villagers go missing
and they're never seen again,

15:09.284 --> 15:10.661
including his last wife.

15:10.744 --> 15:11.912
Oh, God.

15:12.955 --> 15:16.708
I cannot stay here a moment longer.
I want off this dreadful island.

15:16.792 --> 15:20.128
I am but four and ten years almost.
Allow me to wither in my father's attic…

15:20.212 --> 15:22.047
- Sarah. Sarah.
- …as my womanly destiny.

15:22.130 --> 15:23.131
Sarah.

15:25.133 --> 15:28.887
Know that God has chosen you
for a special purpose.

15:30.097 --> 15:33.725
You arrived on this island
not for the reason you thought,

15:33.809 --> 15:35.811
but for a greater one still.

15:36.395 --> 15:39.231
Thou art not alone.

15:41.149 --> 15:43.652
When you retire to bed tonight,

15:45.070 --> 15:48.657
leave the front door unlatched
so that we may enter.

15:49.783 --> 15:50.784
To do what?

15:53.537 --> 15:55.372
What must be done.

15:59.668 --> 16:04.047
No one understands
the burdens of leadership.

16:04.673 --> 16:07.384
They're conspiring against me,
and you know that.

16:07.467 --> 16:10.387
They are afraid.
The plague, the disappearances…

16:10.470 --> 16:11.763
Disappearances?

16:14.641 --> 16:15.893
What disappearances?

16:18.562 --> 16:20.022
Who have you been speaking with?

16:20.105 --> 16:21.315
I've spoken with no one.

16:25.235 --> 16:26.236
'Tis nothing.

16:26.320 --> 16:27.321
I…

16:28.322 --> 16:30.824
Forgive me, I cannot make sense of my own…

16:30.908 --> 16:31.992
My own words.

16:34.953 --> 16:36.622
Take all the children upstairs.

16:37.539 --> 16:38.540
The…

16:39.166 --> 16:40.167
Children.

16:53.722 --> 16:55.140
Is something wrong?

16:58.852 --> 17:00.270
All shall be well.

19:45.811 --> 19:47.813
Did I not plainly forewarn you?

19:50.023 --> 19:52.526
For your own safety,
you must not leave this house again.

19:53.485 --> 19:55.904
Not to do the wash,
not to accompany the children.

20:01.702 --> 20:05.038
Well, let no fear take hold.

20:06.707 --> 20:10.460
I will unearth the one
who bears this guilt.

20:10.544 --> 20:15.966
None may hide forever on an island
where there is no way out.

20:21.263 --> 20:22.431
I will protect us.

20:28.645 --> 20:29.646
Go to our room.

20:30.480 --> 20:31.690
Pray.

20:42.868 --> 20:46.330
Oh, please. Oh, please.
Oh, Father, please.

20:49.041 --> 20:50.042
Please.

24:22.963 --> 24:24.214
Pastor Collins!

24:25.340 --> 24:27.968
Richard is alive!

24:30.846 --> 24:33.724
Yes, we noted that with some distress.

24:35.434 --> 24:37.769
Be not afraid.
This committee can be trusted.

24:37.853 --> 24:39.605
Then you all must listen.

24:39.688 --> 24:41.523
He is not consorting with the devil.

24:41.607 --> 24:43.025
He is the devil.

24:43.108 --> 24:45.944
I saw him struck with a knife again
and again, but he died not.

24:46.028 --> 24:48.864
For the good of every man, woman,
and child, you must make haste

24:48.947 --> 24:50.490
and stop him immediately.

24:53.243 --> 24:54.912
There's a secret tunnel
that leads to the house.

24:54.995 --> 24:58.248
There's a well at the far southeastern
edge that will grant to serve you passage.

24:58.332 --> 25:00.834
You must send ten good, strong men.

25:05.672 --> 25:08.926
A merchant sailing vessel
is due to depart this evening

25:09.009 --> 25:10.886
with a berth for you on it…

25:10.969 --> 25:12.262
God be thanked.

25:12.346 --> 25:15.265
…but we need your help.

25:19.061 --> 25:24.566
Pour this in his drink,
and he will be helpless as a babe.

25:24.650 --> 25:26.652
No, I cannot go back there.

25:26.735 --> 25:29.488
You must, or he shall know.

25:30.364 --> 25:35.202
You said he must be stopped.
Now you bear the burden as well.

25:35.285 --> 25:38.121
Consider the welfare of your children.

25:39.289 --> 25:42.709
My children? I have but just met them.

25:42.793 --> 25:44.795
Sarah, please.

25:45.337 --> 25:49.174
You are our only hope
against this darkness.

25:54.555 --> 25:57.808
I do not comprehend
the nature of the curse

25:57.891 --> 25:59.643
that has fallen on the island.

26:00.435 --> 26:06.608
I do know that its heart beats inside the
cylinder my husband wears around his neck.

26:07.359 --> 26:08.777
Who will crush my throat?

26:08.861 --> 26:11.905
His hands? This plague?

26:11.989 --> 26:15.993
Death comes for us each,
but I fear to me first.

26:16.785 --> 26:18.620
I know not how, but who.

26:28.505 --> 26:33.427
Of course, he's here with me,
so I say all this in jest.

26:34.011 --> 26:36.096
And with that, I retire.

26:46.481 --> 26:48.066
You're home. What a blessing.

26:49.735 --> 26:51.778
What do you write in that book?

26:53.071 --> 26:54.781
A woman's silly thoughts.

26:56.700 --> 26:57.951
I want to read it.

26:59.244 --> 27:00.829
I would feel too abashed.

27:28.315 --> 27:30.317
A swig of brandy to ease your mind.

27:32.194 --> 27:34.112
No, I need to be clearheaded.

27:41.537 --> 27:42.913
Go to your beds now, children.

27:42.996 --> 27:46.083
Now. I need a quiet word with your father.

27:47.668 --> 27:48.669
Now.

28:05.853 --> 28:11.775
If folk are truly set against you,
you need your wife at your side.

28:15.904 --> 28:18.365
We are married all these days
and have not yet…

28:21.285 --> 28:22.452
known each other.

28:28.333 --> 28:32.796
Well, the burdens that have
been placed upon me--

28:32.880 --> 28:34.882
Let me help you bear them.

29:08.040 --> 29:09.958
What sin lies on your tongue?

29:12.961 --> 29:16.089
You're in league with them. Traitress.

29:31.563 --> 29:32.731
He killed my mother.

29:35.025 --> 29:36.944
Gather your siblings. We're leaving.

29:44.201 --> 29:45.452
Who are they?

29:45.536 --> 29:46.703
Just keep moving.

30:09.434 --> 30:10.644
They left without us.

30:11.854 --> 30:14.273
Here, into this boat. We can catch them.

30:14.982 --> 30:15.983
Easy.

30:23.365 --> 30:24.908
Are you leaving?

30:27.202 --> 30:28.412
Abigail, I…

30:29.454 --> 30:31.290
I reckon you are not well.

30:31.957 --> 30:33.584
Go to your husband, the physician.

30:34.585 --> 30:35.794
I did already.

30:39.464 --> 30:41.258
I will get on board with you.

30:41.341 --> 30:43.427
I'm sorry, there is not enough space.

30:45.095 --> 30:46.680
But I am not sick!

30:48.557 --> 30:50.142
Forgive me, there is no space.

30:50.684 --> 30:53.520
Then leave off these children.
They're not of thy blood.

30:56.064 --> 30:57.065
They're with me.

30:59.526 --> 31:01.069
And under my charge.

31:03.780 --> 31:07.451
Stand back! I will take no more orders!

31:18.295 --> 31:21.381
Go. Go. The ropes.

31:35.896 --> 31:37.022
Traitors.

31:40.234 --> 31:44.071
You've set yourself above
the law of God and man.

31:44.154 --> 31:48.158
You have murdered
those you swore to protect.

31:49.368 --> 31:50.369
No!

31:51.036 --> 31:53.163
It doesn't want you to open it.

31:53.247 --> 31:55.791
What does not want me to open it?

31:56.375 --> 31:58.126
That which has kept us alive.

31:59.127 --> 32:02.965
It is just as we feared.
You have made a deal with the devil.

32:03.048 --> 32:05.217
No, it's not the devil.

32:05.843 --> 32:07.427
It is our God.

32:07.511 --> 32:10.931
He's gone mad. Let us be rid of him.

32:11.014 --> 32:12.516
You cannot rid yourself of me.

32:13.517 --> 32:15.018
It won't allow it.

32:15.102 --> 32:17.521
This is my burden.

32:18.438 --> 32:23.402
Free me, you will all be forgiven,
and I will continue to carry it myself.

32:23.485 --> 32:29.199
Your fate will be decided by God,
the one true God.

32:37.040 --> 32:42.004
No. You cannot bury me!
You cannot bury me!

32:43.380 --> 32:45.883
You'll doom yourselves! The pact!

32:46.383 --> 32:48.218
The pact must be honored!

32:48.302 --> 32:51.847
The pact which spared us…
in that first winter.

32:52.431 --> 32:55.017
It spoke to me through the mushrooms!

32:56.101 --> 32:58.353
Please. Fulfill the pact.

32:58.437 --> 32:59.646
How?

32:59.730 --> 33:01.773
Sacrifice! A life…

33:01.857 --> 33:02.858
Life for life.

33:04.276 --> 33:09.448
Whatever I have undertaken,
it has been for the welfare of our people!

33:10.282 --> 33:14.953
Fulfill the pact and the plague will stop!

33:15.913 --> 33:17.122
But if you don't…

33:17.706 --> 33:18.832
If you do not,

33:20.417 --> 33:22.544
the terrors will not cease!

33:22.628 --> 33:24.254
They will only deepen!

33:24.338 --> 33:28.383
Please do not make my children
suffer for your mistake.

33:29.051 --> 33:33.055
Your wife is taking your children
back to the mainland, far from you.

33:34.848 --> 33:37.226
No. No, no, no.

33:37.309 --> 33:39.645
The island won't…
The island won't let them leave.

33:40.562 --> 33:42.314
Oh, please! Oh, please!

33:42.397 --> 33:44.441
You'll kill them all!
You'll kill them all!

33:48.820 --> 33:51.615
You'll kill them all!

33:51.698 --> 33:56.203
You'll kill them all!
You'll kill them all!

33:56.286 --> 33:58.330
You'll kill them all!

33:58.997 --> 34:03.752
You'll kill them all!
You'll kill them all!

34:03.836 --> 34:07.005
You'll kill them all!

35:23.332 --> 35:24.333
I got it.

35:27.920 --> 35:29.505
- You got it?
- Come on.
